{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And now, O Israel, what does HaShem your Elohim ask of you but to fear.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Berakhot 33a): 'And is fear such a small thing? Yes, for Moses it was a small thing.' And they raise the difficulty here: was it for this reason that He said to all Israel, \"What does HaShem ask of you\"? And there are those who answer: for Moses — that is, when Israel were with Moses, for he would guide them in the trait of fear — then it was a small thing. And I say that this is the intent of the verse when it says \"And now, O Israel\": what is \"and now\"? Rather, because afterward it is said: ״וִידַעְתֶּם הַיּוֹם כִּי לֹא אֶת בְּנֵיכֶם אֲשֶׁר לֹא יָדְעוּ וְלֹא רָאוּ אֶת מוּסַר ה׳ אֱלֹהֵיכֶם״ and so on, and the entire passage until ״עֵינֵיכֶם הָרֹאוֹת אֶת כָּל מַעֲשֵׂה ה׳״ and so on — this is its explanation: had I demanded fear from your children who will arise after you, who did not see all the awesome deeds that HaShem did, so that His fear might be upon their faces — then indeed I would have been asking a great thing, for it is certainly difficult to bring a person under the yoke of fear, for it is great. But \"and now\" — meaning this generation: you have seen (Jeremiah 2:31), for with your own eyes you saw all the awesome deeds that Elohim did so that they would fear before Him, and you are already accustomed to the trait of fear; therefore \"and now,\" inasmuch as it is present with you, a small thing is what HaShem asks of you. And this is what they said 'for Moses' — this is the wilderness generation, who were in the time of Moses; for them fear is certainly a small thing, and from fear one comes to the rung of love. This is what it says: ״וּלְאַהֲבָה אֹתוֹ״. And he concludes ״לְטוֹב לָךְ״, that is, the receiving of reward, as Rashi interpreted; and he mentioned it at the end to say that the ultimate reward comes of itself, and should not be the initial intent of your actions, for the sake of receiving a prize."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:11:49.429720566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}